HotpotQA Evaluation Script — Attribution and Licensing
========================================================

This directory contains a vendored / faithfully-reimplemented copy of the
HotpotQA reference answer-evaluation logic for use inside the Aether
benchmark suite.

Source
------

Upstream file:
    https://github.com/hotpotqa/hotpot/blob/master/hotpot_evaluate_v1.py

Upstream repository:
    https://github.com/hotpotqa/hotpot

Paper:
    Yang et al., "HotpotQA: A Dataset for Diverse, Explainable Multi-hop
    Question Answering", EMNLP 2018. https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.09600

Vendored on:
    2026-05-08

What was vendored
-----------------

Only the answer-evaluation primitives required by the bench harness:

  * normalize_answer(s)         — SQuAD/HotpotQA-style string normalisation
  * f1_score(pred, gold)        — token-level F1 with yes/no/noanswer guard
  * exact_match_score(pred, gold) — boolean EM after normalisation
  * update_answer(metrics, ...) — accumulator helper
  * evaluate_predictions(preds, golds) — convenience aggregator

Supporting-facts (sentence-level) and joint metrics from the upstream
script are intentionally NOT vendored — the bench harness does not yet
score sentence-level supporting facts.

Licensing
---------

The HotpotQA upstream code repository (https://github.com/hotpotqa/hotpot)
does NOT carry a top-level LICENSE file at the time of vendoring.

The HotpotQA dataset itself is distributed under
    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
    (CC BY-SA 4.0)
per the project page: https://hotpotqa.github.io/

This vendored implementation reproduces the standard SQuAD-style
normalisation pipeline (lower / strip-punct / drop-articles /
collapse-whitespace) followed by token F1 / EM. That algorithm is
well-documented in both the HotpotQA paper (above) and the SQuAD paper
(Rajpurkar et al., EMNLP 2016, https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.05250) and is
broadly considered the reference HotpotQA metric.

If the upstream HotpotQA project later publishes a LICENSE that imposes
additional terms on the evaluation script, this vendored copy should be
updated to comply or replaced with a re-fetched canonical copy.

